    nif:isString "Indian copper falls , state firm may cut rates .  BOMBAY 1996-08-30  Indian copper prices fell on Friday as dealers awaited an announcement relating to price cuts by state-owned producer , Hindustan Copper Ltd , traders said .  Nickel extended gains while other base metals were unchanged in narrow trade , they said .  Ready copper fell by 150 rupees at 12,350 rupees per quintal on fresh offerings by the stockists who expect Hindustan Copper to cut prices .  Nickel rose by 500 to 39,200 rupees on thin supply and fresh buying by stainless steel makers .  Tin was unchanged at 36,000 rupees , so did zinc at 6,300 rupees and lead at 4,900 rupees .  Aluminium was quiet at 7,450 rupees .  -- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000 " .

<https://anonymiz.ed/AIDA-YAGO2-dataset/7e916ba450a24f08eb440ec97993b97988652807ee2a02aba5633c4e79174b2f> a nif:Context,
