    nif:endIndex "662"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    nif:isString "S. Korea asked to stop China-bound missionaries .  BEIJING 1996-08-27  Beijing has called on Seoul to stop South Korean missionaries from travelling to China , a South Korean embassy spokesman said on Tuesday .  The appeal was made on Sunday during talks between South Korean deputy Foreign Minister Lee Ki-choo and his Chinese counterpart Tang Jiaxuan , the spokesman said .  It is not known why China raised the issue .  Atheist China officially bans missionary activities but often turns a blind eye to religious activities of people nominally employed as foreign language teachers , particularly in remote areas that are unable to attract other candidates . " .

