    nif:isString "Electronic Data bags flight data contract .  LONDON 1996-12-06  Information technology firm Electronic Data Systems said on Friday it had bagged a contract for the first air traffic control project being funded under the Private Finance Initiative .  In a statement , EDS said the contract would be in the region of 50 million stg .  The contract involved upgrading the flight data processing system at the Oceanic Control Centre in Prestwick in south west Scotland for National Air Traffic Services Ltd ( NATS ) , subsidiary of the Civil Aviation Authority .  The system is responsible for the control of aircraft flying transatlantic routes from Europe and North America .  The system , which would use satellite technology , is scheduled to enter service in 2000 .  -- London Newsroom +44-171-542 7717 " .

<https://anonymiz.ed/AIDA-YAGO2-dataset/9b18407189b1a710d1faa1f234e16dd241dfe370ed024b040dab6577d1ac889a> a nif:Context,
