    nif:isString "Denmark 's Radiometer H1 result seen flat .  COPENHAGEN 1996-12-06  A Reuter consensus survey sees medical equipment group Radiometer reporting largely unchanged earnings when it publishes first half 19996/97 results next Wednesday .  An average of four analysts ' forecasts predicted pre-tax profit of 147.3 million crowns compared to 144.5 million in the first six months of 1995/96 .  They said that the group 's failure to introduce new products was behind the share 's weak performance in 1996 , during which it has lost seven percent so far .  -- Soeren Linding Jakobsen , Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650 " .

<https://anonymiz.ed/AIDA-YAGO2-dataset/ae23ee84e6c65c81ff095a6d2cf5d7d9fddbad31e0e51e812ce43bc9d710af0e> a nif:Context,
