    nif:endIndex "754"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    nif:isString "SIMEX Nikkei ends down but off lows .  SINGAPORE 1996-08-29  Simex Nikkei futures ended easier but off the day 's lows on Thursday .  Dealers said selling in the session was a follow-through from Wednesday 's gloomy Tankan corporate report by the Bank of Japan .  \" The Nikkei is testing support at the 20,500 level .  Sentiment is a bit gloomy because people are focusing on the weak recovery in the economy at the moment , \" said a dealer with a European bank .  September Nikkei settled at 20,605 after touching an intraday low of 20,530 against its previous close of 20,725 .  Volume was 19,560 contracts .  Dealers said technically , the index should see good support at 20,300 and the upside should be capped at 21,000 .  -- Doreen Siow 65-8703092 " .

<https://anonymiz.ed/AIDA-YAGO2-dataset/c64add112aaa82ffb9773b306bb52519be6f466ad3360ea6679dae54e8e50b61> a nif:Context,
