    nif:isString "Senegal cholera outbreak kills five .  DAKAR 1996-08-22  An outbreak of cholera has killed five people in the central Senegal town of Kaolack , where health authorities have recorded 291 cases since August 11 , a medical official said on Thursday .  Doctor Masserigne Ndiaye said medical staff were overwhelmed with work . \"  People are rushing to the hospital as soon as the first symptoms appear , that 's why we have fewer deaths , \" he told Reuters by telephone from the town , 160 km ( 100 miles ) southeast of the Senegalese capital Dakar . " .

<https://anonymiz.ed/AIDA-YAGO2-dataset/d02c21d6d0c2d5d4bec90b70cb84845a17e2b4c83966288348c169ec5bd41932> a nif:Context,
