    nif:isString "PRESS DIGEST - Iraq - Aug 24 .  BAGHDAD 1996-08-24  These are some of the leading stories in the official Iraqi press on Saturday .  Reuters has not verified these stories and does not vouch for their accuracy .  JUMHOURIYA  - Istanbul chamber of commerce urges Ankara to resume trade with Iraq .  - Offers from Arab and foreign companies to supply Iraq with goods .  - Four ships unload tonnes of Iraq-bound sugar at Jordan 's Aqaba .  - Editorial blames U.S. for latest flare-up of fighting between Kurdish rebels in northern Iraq .  - Black market booms in the shadow of state-run supermarkets .  - Parliament completes draft law on protection of river waters in Iraq .  QADISSIYA  - Iraq denounces violation of airspace by U.S. warplanes .  IRAQ  - Editorial lambasts Jalal Talabani , leader of a Kurdish rebel faction in the north , for liaising with Iran in its fight against rivals .  BABEL  - Blaming Iraq for riots in Jordan is a dirty game . " .

