    nif:endIndex "555"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    nif:isString "Thieves make off with cash from prison canteen .  LIMERICK , Ireland 1996-08-29  Thieves stole almost 2,000 Irish pounds ( $ 3,000 ) from the officers ' canteen of a Limerick jail on Thursday while warders slept in a room upstairs .  Police said the thieves intercepted a woman arriving to work at the canteen , forced her to open the safe where takings were kept and made off with the cash .  While the robbery was going on , several officers were asleep in a room over the canteen , which is in the grounds of the prison on Ireland 's southwest coast . " .

