    nif:isString "Canada 's international travel account gap shrinks .  OTTAWA 1996-08-29  Higher spending by foreign visitors and less Canadian tourist spending abroad cut the deficit in Canada 's international travel account by 26.5 percent in the second quarter , Statistics Canada said on Thursday .  The deficit fell to a seasonally adjusted C$ 715 million in the second quarter from C$ 973 million in the first , as foreigners spent a record C$ 3.00 billion seasonally adjusted while Canadians reduced their spending abroad by 5.1 percent to C$ 3.72 billion .  -- Reuters Ottawa Burea ( 613 ) 235-6745 " .

<https://anonymiz.ed/AIDA-YAGO2-dataset/f191064eac936e958cdca552a14a2b3019005ff09706233b414682a176c0c50a> a nif:Context,
