    nif:isString "Promodes set to sell German assets - paper .  PARIS 1996-08-23  German retailer Promodes is in advanced talks about selling its German assets and the retailer 's board might decide as soon as Tuesday to sell the assets to Spar AG , Les Echos newspaper said on Friday .  It said investment bank Rothschild & Cie was an intermediary in the talks and added that unlisted German retailers Metro , Rewe and Lidl were also still in discussions .  Promodes has in Germany its Promo hypermarket unit with 36 Continent superstores , which is 1995 generated 4.7 percent of total Promodes sales .  The French group entered the German market in 1990 , buying  In June , Promodes signed an outline agreement to sell its Specia unit -- which runs 100 Dia stores in France -- to Germany 's Aldi .  Promodes was not immediately available for comment .  -- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 " .

<https://anonymiz.ed/AIDA-YAGO2-dataset/fe125bf538762f14ffdc39f76ae6181bc6e4e3018e5dee33220e196b44ed3a9c> a nif:Context,
